condition_name: Hypothyroidism (Myxoedema)
condition_slug: hypothyroidism-myxoedema
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A state of subnormal concentration of thyroid hormones in the circulation is called hypothyroidism. The extreme form of hypothyroidism is referred to as myxoedema.
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Adults
    features[10]: "Dull facial expression, slow speech and poor memory","Puffiness of the hands, feet and face",Lethargy and fatigue,"Thinning, dryness and loss of hair",Hypothermia,"Bradycardia, reduced systolic and increased diastolic blood pressure",Weight gain,Decreased reflexes,Constipation,Menstrual abnormalities
  - type: Infants
    features[2]: Mental and physical retardation,"If not corrected, cretinism"
investigations[3]: Total serum T3 and T4 levels,TSH stimulation test,TRH test
treatment:
  goals[4]: Establish cause,Establish the severity of hypothyroidism,Restore normal body functions,Prevent Complications
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[2]: Levothyroxine sodium (thyroxine sodium) for adults and children with specific dosages,Liothyronine sodium (1-tri-iodothyronine sodium) for adults and children with specific dosages
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[2]: Thyroxine should not be used alone for long term replacement therapy,Monitor serum levels of hormones to ensure that patients are not exposed to cardiac risks
  supportive_measures[2]: "Treat anaemia, constipation and other complications as appropriate",Immediate mechanical ventilation in myxoedema coma
differential_diagnoses[2]: Endogenous depression,Reactive depression
complications[1]: Myxoedema coma in adults and cretinism in the young
prevention[1]: Iodinated salt to prevent iodine deficiency
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null